<title>BRAZIL: Brazil posts $951 mln trade gap in April.</title>
<headline>Brazil posts $951 mln trade gap in April.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil posted a $951 million trade gap in April, with exports of $4.629 billion and imports of $5.580 billion, the Ministry of Industry and Commerce said in a statement.</p>
<p>The month saw average daily imports of $265.7 million and average daily exports of $220.4 million, the statement said.</p>
<p>The deficit was above market expectations for a $750 million to $800 million trade gap.</p>
<p>((-- John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414))</p>
